# neck/scarf: the scarf (A3's hero): the wrap and knot; the tail hangs at rest and flies in side walks (neck keys)
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY); A3's pixels are the reference (docs/ref/style_a3). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# GARB-W (wave 2): fitted to the man only (his collar row is F-19); the woman wears her own, neck/woman/scarf.
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2) `when layer-scarf replace` views: the scarf over armour (STYLE_P2 28.3's over-layer SCARF): the knot on the gorget and the ends 4-5 rows down the chest facing D, streaming 4-6 px behind in the walk and the run; generated by FORGE-MANTLE gen/scarf.py.
use person
body man
role neck scarf
layer neck
anchor neck
keys neck
# (FORGE-MANTLE, round 2 i3) `when layer-scarf,!beard replace`: the same scarf on layer headwear, so a camail, veil, bevor or neck guard never swallows it (a beard still lies over it: the plain `layer-scarf` views below).

view D key rest origin 5 0
|mpnnnnnnom
|.mponnnm..

view U key rest origin 5 0
|mpooooonnm

view R key flow origin 12 0
|.....mnmpooonnm
|-moonnnn.......
|.m--...m.......

